{"title":"Career Roadmap · PET-CT Technologist","role":"PET-CT Technologist","summary":"A PET-CT Technologist operates and supports PET-CT imaging procedures used primarily for oncology and other clinical applications. The role combines nuclear medicine, radiopharmaceutical handling, CT imaging, patient preparation, radiation safety, image acquisition, equipment operation, and clinical workflow.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Nuclear Medicine Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A PET-CT Technologist operates and supports PET-CT imaging procedures used primarily for oncology and other clinical applications. The role combines nuclear medicine, radiopharmaceutical handling, CT imaging, patient preparation, radiation safety, image acquisition, equipment operation, and clinical workflow."},{"type":"p","text":"This is a specialized allied-health pathway. The exact eligibility and scope of practice depend on the institution, program, clinical regulations, and applicable Indian requirements. A generic B.Sc alone does not automatically qualify someone to independently perform PET-CT procedures; students should select a recognized Nuclear Medicine Technology / Medical Imaging / relevant allied-health program whose curriculum specifically provides PET-CT and clinical training."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","Typical Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Clinical Foundation"},{"text":"Undergraduate training → Clinical internship"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"PET-CT Practice"},{"text":"PET-CT Technologist / Nuclear Medicine Technologist"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Advanced Imaging"},{"text":"Senior Technologist / Specialized Imaging Technologist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Leadership / Applications"},{"text":"Chief Technologist / Imaging Coordinator / Applications Specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"Build the Academic Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Basic Medical & Imaging Sciences"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Human sciences"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"First aid"},{"text":"Clinical communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Physics foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atomic structure"},{"text":"Radiation"},{"text":"Radioactivity"},{"text":"Nuclear decay"},{"text":"Half-life"},{"text":"Radiation interaction with matter"},{"text":"Detection of radiation"},{"text":"Basic imaging physics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Nuclear Medicine Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the core academic stage."},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nuclear medicine principles"},{"text":"Radiopharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Radioisotopes"},{"text":"Gamma radiation"},{"text":"Positron emission"},{"text":"Annihilation photons"},{"text":"Radiation detectors"},{"text":"Scintillation"},{"text":"Gamma cameras"},{"text":"SPECT"},{"text":"PET"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the basic PET principle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Radiopharmaceutical","Patient Administration","Tracer Distribution","Positron Emission","Annihilation","Two 511 keV Photons","PET Detector Ring","Image Reconstruction"]},{"type":"h","text":"PET-CT Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand that PET-CT combines:"},{"type":"h","text":"PET → functional/metabolic information"},{"type":"p","text":"with"},{"type":"h","text":"CT → anatomical information"},{"type":"p","text":"Conceptually:"},{"type":"p","text":"PET"},{"type":"p","text":"Functional / Metabolic Information"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"CT"},{"type":"flow","items":["Anatomical Information","PET-CT Study","Fused Imaging"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PET acquisition"},{"text":"CT acquisition"},{"text":"Image fusion"},{"text":"Attenuation correction"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Motion considerations"},{"text":"Basic image artifacts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Radiopharmaceuticals"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of commonly used radiopharmaceutical concepts."},{"type":"p","text":"Particularly understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radionuclide"},{"text":"Radiopharmaceutical"},{"text":"Tracer"},{"text":"Activity"},{"text":"Half-life"},{"text":"Administration"},{"text":"Biodistribution"},{"text":"Uptake"},{"text":"Clearance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A commonly encountered PET tracer is 18F-FDG, particularly in oncology imaging."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand its basic clinical principle without treating PET uptake as diagnostic by itself."},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"Radiation safety is one of the most important competencies."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"ALARA principle"},{"text":"Radiation monitoring"},{"text":"Personal dosimetry"},{"text":"Contamination prevention"},{"text":"Controlled areas"},{"text":"Radiation warning systems"},{"text":"Safe handling procedures"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic principle"},{"type":"p","text":"Reduce Time"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Increase Distance"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Use Appropriate Shielding","Reduce Radiation Exposure"]},{"type":"p","text":"The student must follow the institution's radiation-safety procedures and applicable regulatory requirements rather than relying on informal practices."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — CT Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Because the target role involves PET-CT, CT knowledge is essential."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT scanner components"},{"text":"X-ray generation"},{"text":"Detectors"},{"text":"Gantry"},{"text":"Table movement"},{"text":"Helical scanning"},{"text":"Slice thickness"},{"text":"Pitch"},{"text":"Reconstruction"},{"text":"CT numbers / Hounsfield units"},{"text":"Contrast fundamentals"},{"text":"CT artifacts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how changing acquisition parameters affects:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Radiation dose"},{"text":"Scan time"}]},{"type":"h","text":"PET Image Acquisition"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Fasting requirements"},{"text":"Blood glucose assessment"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Radiopharmaceutical administration"},{"text":"Uptake period"},{"text":"Scan acquisition"},{"text":"Motion management"},{"text":"Image quality checks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A simplified workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Preparation","Clinical Verification","Radiopharmaceutical Administration","Uptake Period","Patient Positioning","CT Acquisition","PET Acquisition","Image Reconstruction","Quality Check","Study Transfer"]},{"type":"p","text":"Exact protocols vary according to the tracer, clinical indication, equipment and institutional protocol."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Patient Care"},{"type":"p","text":"A PET-CT Technologist works directly with patients."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"Clinical history verification"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Mobility assistance"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Privacy"},{"text":"Consent workflow"},{"text":"Monitoring during procedures"},{"text":"Recognition of basic emergencies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Pay particular attention to patients who may be:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Elderly"},{"text":"Pediatric"},{"text":"Claustrophobic"},{"text":"Physically impaired"},{"text":"Seriously ill"},{"text":"Unable to remain still"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Contrast & Safety Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Where contrast-enhanced CT is performed, understand the technologist's role in the institutional workflow for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient screening"},{"text":"Allergy history"},{"text":"Renal-function information as required by protocol"},{"text":"IV access"},{"text":"Contrast administration under authorized procedures"},{"text":"Adverse-reaction recognition"},{"text":"Emergency escalation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A technologist should not independently make clinical decisions outside their authorized scope."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Clinical Training & Advanced Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical exposure becomes the most important component."},{"type":"p","text":"Gain supervised experience in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PET-CT"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine"},{"text":"Gamma camera"},{"text":"SPECT/SPECT-CT"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Radiopharmaceutical workflow"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"CT acquisition"},{"text":"Image quality control"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Image Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to recognize common technical problems."},{"type":"h","text":"PET"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand effects of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient movement"},{"text":"Incorrect positioning"},{"text":"Low tracer uptake"},{"text":"Injection problems"},{"text":"Extravasation"},{"text":"Incorrect acquisition"},{"text":"Reconstruction issues"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CT"},{"type":"p","text":"Recognize:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion artifacts"},{"text":"Metal artifacts"},{"text":"Beam-hardening"},{"text":"Incorrect positioning"},{"text":"Truncation"},{"text":"Poor contrast timing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist's responsibility is generally to identify and address technical problems within scope and escalate clinical interpretation to the appropriate physician."},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Control"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand routine equipment and imaging quality-control concepts."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Detector performance"},{"text":"Image uniformity"},{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Sensitivity"},{"text":"Equipment checks"},{"text":"Daily/periodic QC"},{"text":"CT quality assurance"},{"text":"Dose monitoring"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Students should learn the specific QC protocols of the equipment and institution during clinical training."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Imaging Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"PACS"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Image storage"},{"text":"Image retrieval"},{"text":"Study transfer"},{"text":"Worklists"}]},{"type":"h","text":"RIS"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient scheduling"},{"text":"Examination information"},{"text":"Reporting workflow"}]},{"type":"h","text":"DICOM"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical image format"},{"text":"Image transfer"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Modality communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data & Technology Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"A modern PET-CT Technologist benefits from basic technology skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Healthcare information systems"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"DICOM fundamentals"},{"text":"Data documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Optional:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Medical image analysis concepts"},{"text":"AI imaging fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Programming is not normally a core requirement for entry-level clinical practice."},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Projects"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — PET-CT Workflow Optimization"},{"type":"p","text":"Map the patient workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Registration","Patient Screening","Preparation","Tracer Administration","Uptake","CT","PET","Quality Check","PACS"]},{"type":"p","text":"Identify possible delays and propose workflow improvements."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Radiation Safety Audit"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an educational audit covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Dosimetry"},{"text":"Controlled areas"},{"text":"PPE where applicable"},{"text":"Contamination procedures"},{"text":"Emergency response"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use institutional/regulatory guidance as the reference standard."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — PET-CT Image Quality Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare simulated or approved teaching datasets for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion"},{"text":"Noise"},{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Attenuation"},{"text":"Positioning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Document the effect of technical factors on image quality."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — CT Dose & Image Quality Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Study how acquisition parameters influence:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation dose"},{"text":"Noise"},{"text":"Spatial resolution"},{"text":"Image quality"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The project should use approved educational datasets or phantom data rather than exposing patient information."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Digital Nuclear Medicine Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a workflow integrating:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Registration","RIS","PET-CT","DICOM","PACS","Radiologist / Nuclear Medicine Physician","Report"]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship / Clinical Training Strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, clinical training is more important than conventional corporate internships."},{"type":"p","text":"Seek supervised clinical exposure in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nuclear medicine departments"},{"text":"PET-CT centers"},{"text":"Oncology hospitals"},{"text":"Medical imaging centers"},{"text":"Teaching hospitals"},{"text":"Academic medical centers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important clinical exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"Try to gain experience with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PET-CT workflow"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine procedures"},{"text":"Radiopharmaceutical handling under supervision"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"CT acquisition"},{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should maintain a structured clinical logbook where required by the program."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist"},{"text":"PET-CT Technologist"},{"text":"Nuclear Medicine Imaging Technologist"},{"text":"PET Technologist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"With the appropriate qualification and scope:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT Technologist"},{"text":"Medical Imaging Technologist"},{"text":"PET-CT Imaging Technologist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Industry"},{"type":"p","text":"With additional experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical Applications Specialist"},{"text":"Imaging Equipment Applications Specialist"},{"text":"Technical Support Specialist"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact title and eligibility depend on the qualification and employer."},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Requirement","Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"PET-CT operation"},{"text":"PET + CT"}],[{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Patient care"}],[{"text":"Radiopharmaceutical workflow"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine"}],[{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"ALARA + dosimetry"}],[{"text":"Image acquisition"},{"text":"PET/CT protocols"}],[{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Artifact recognition"}],[{"text":"Equipment QC"},{"text":"Quality assurance"}],[{"text":"Digital imaging"},{"text":"PACS/RIS/DICOM"}],[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Clinical communication"}],[{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Basic emergency awareness"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Clinical records"}],[{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Hospital protocols"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine technology"},{"text":"PET-CT applications"},{"text":"CT imaging"},{"text":"Basic life support"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"Medical imaging quality assurance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For regulated clinical roles, the student should prioritize recognized academic qualifications and institution-approved clinical training over private short-course certificates."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After an appropriate undergraduate qualification, possible advanced-study directions can include programs in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nuclear Medicine Technology"},{"text":"Medical Imaging Technology"},{"text":"Radiological Sciences"},{"text":"Medical Imaging"},{"text":"Healthcare Technology"},{"text":"Healthcare Administration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Eligibility varies considerably by institution and program."},{"type":"p","text":"For an imaging-focused career, advanced education should be selected based on the student's underlying recognized qualification and the scope of the desired role."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"}]},{"heading":"PET-CT","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PET acquisition"},{"text":"CT acquisition"},{"text":"Oncology imaging"},{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Radiation safety"}]}]},{"heading":"SPECT / SPECT-CT","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gamma-camera imaging"},{"text":"SPECT"},{"text":"SPECT-CT"},{"text":"Cardiac imaging"},{"text":"Bone imaging"},{"text":"Functional imaging"}]}]},{"heading":"Nuclear Medicine","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Broader exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diagnostic nuclear medicine"},{"text":"Radiopharmaceutical workflows"},{"text":"Gamma imaging"},{"text":"SPECT"},{"text":"PET"}]}]},{"heading":"Imaging Applications","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"With clinical experience, transition toward:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equipment applications"},{"text":"Protocol support"},{"text":"Clinical training"},{"text":"Product demonstrations"},{"text":"Customer applications support"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This can lead to Clinical Applications Specialist roles with medical-imaging technology companies."}]},{"heading":"Imaging Informatics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A technology-oriented route combining:"},{"type":"p","text":"Medical Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"PACS"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"RIS"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"DICOM"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Healthcare IT"},{"type":"p","text":"This can lead toward healthcare-imaging informatics roles with additional training."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Clinical route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Relevant UG Qualification","Clinical Training","PET-CT Technologist","Senior PET-CT Technologist","Lead Technologist","Chief / Department Technologist"]},{"type":"h","text":"Applications route"},{"type":"flow","items":["PET-CT Technologist","Clinical Applications Specialist","Senior Applications Specialist","Applications Manager","Regional / National Applications Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Informatics route"},{"type":"flow","items":["PET-CT Technologist","Imaging Informatics Training","PACS / Imaging Informatics Specialist","Senior Imaging Informatics Professional","Imaging IT / Informatics Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Exact career progression varies by employer, qualification, clinical experience and applicable professional requirements."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"PET-CT is increasingly influenced by:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted image reconstruction"},{"text":"AI-based lesion detection"},{"text":"Automated segmentation"},{"text":"Low-dose imaging"},{"text":"Digital PET"},{"text":"Total-body PET"},{"text":"Motion correction"},{"text":"Quantitative PET"},{"text":"Automated workflow optimization"},{"text":"Radiomics"},{"text":"Imaging biomarkers"},{"text":"Advanced PACS"},{"text":"Cloud-based imaging"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A future-ready technologist should understand how AI affects image acquisition, reconstruction, quality control and workflow, while recognizing that clinical interpretation remains the responsibility of appropriately qualified clinicians."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"p","text":"Anatomy"},{"type":"p","text":"Physiology"},{"type":"p","text":"Patient Care"},{"type":"p","text":"Infection Control"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical Communication"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine"},{"type":"p","text":"Nuclear Medicine"},{"type":"p","text":"Radiopharmaceuticals"},{"type":"p","text":"PET"},{"type":"p","text":"SPECT"},{"type":"p","text":"Radiation Physics"},{"type":"p","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"h","text":"PET-CT"},{"type":"p","text":"PET Acquisition"},{"type":"p","text":"CT Acquisition"},{"type":"p","text":"Image Fusion"},{"type":"p","text":"Attenuation Correction"},{"type":"p","text":"Image Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Artifact Recognition"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"PACS"},{"type":"p","text":"RIS"},{"type":"p","text":"DICOM"},{"type":"p","text":"Healthcare IT"},{"type":"p","text":"Basic Data Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"p","text":"AI Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Quantitative PET"},{"type":"p","text":"Radiomics"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital PET"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced Image Reconstruction"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By the end of clinical training, the student should understand the complete supervised PET-CT workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Identification","Clinical / Safety Screening","Patient Preparation","Radiopharmaceutical Workflow","Uptake Period","Patient Positioning","CT Acquisition","PET Acquisition","Image Reconstruction","Technical Quality Check","PACS Transfer","Physician Interpretation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should ideally graduate with a recognized relevant qualification, substantial supervised clinical training, PET-CT and nuclear-medicine fundamentals, strong radiation-safety knowledge, CT competency, patient-care skills, and PACS/RIS/DICOM familiarity."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"Nuclear Medicine Technology → PET-CT Technologist is a specialized clinical imaging pathway rather than a generic allied-health job. The strongest employability combination is Nuclear Medicine + PET + CT + Radiation Safety + Patient Care + Image Quality + Clinical Workflow."},{"type":"p","text":"For long-term growth, the student can specialize in advanced PET-CT, SPECT/CT, nuclear medicine, imaging applications, or imaging informatics. The most future-ready profile combines strong clinical imaging competency with healthcare IT and AI-imaging awareness, creating a pathway from PET-CT Technologist → Senior Technologist → Lead/Chief Technologist or Clinical Applications Specialist."}]}]}